From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Murray <81541646+RyanTheTide@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 02:54:46 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] media: apple: scaler: build the register list for same-size
 jobs

Add the job builder the submission path will use: it turns a source
image, a destination image and an optional colour matrix into the
ordered register writes for one job, ending with the pre-start tag and
START. It covers conversions without scaling, which are the common case
(decoder output to RGB, RGB to encoder input):

- read and write DMA: layout, format code, subsampling, plane addresses,
  strides, component order, picture and per-plane sizes;
- alpha fill when the source has no alpha and the destination does;
- chroma upsampling for 4:2:x sources and downsampling for 4:2:x
  destinations, ordered dither when going from 10 to 8 bits;
- the scaler at 1:1 (filters off, unit Q22 ratios);
- the CSC matrix, offsets and clamps;
- the per-plane memory request words and control words the engine is
  driven with on every job.

KUnit builds three 1080p jobs (NV12 BT.709 to ARGB32, ARGB32 to NV12,
P010 BT.2020 to ARGB32) and checks that every register ends with the
value the engine was given for the same job on macOS, and that nothing
else is written.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Ryan Murray <81541646+RyanTheTide@users.noreply.github.com>
(cherry picked from commit 2fb8a25a57e40f3b7dc49c7d6e875f677b424552)
